wlroots 0.20: render with the stock Android EGL/GLES through libhybris (B8000-H, G5)

- render/egl.c: libhybris has no EGL client extensions: default display,
  RGBA8888 config, surfaceless context; fake XRGB/ARGB8888 render formats.
- render/allocator/hybris.c: gralloc buffers (EGL_HYBRIS_native_buffer),
  exposed as a single-plane DMA-BUF (the ION fd) for KMS scan-out.
- gles2: render into EGL_NATIVE_BUFFER_ANDROID images (texture fallback),
  no DMA-BUF texture formats (clients stay on wl_shm), glFinish before
  scan-out (no implicit fences), uploads without GL_EXT_unpack_subimage,
  GL_KHR_debug off (the driver logs every eglMakeCurrent).

- gles2 textures from 32-bit shm buffers live in linear gralloc buffers
  sampled through EGLImages: updates are memcpy of the damage (5-7 ms per
  1280x800 frame, 0.3 ms per 100-row band; glTexSubImage2D: 18 / 7 ms).
- read_pixels (screencopy, phosh thumbnails) of ARGB/XRGB8888 without
  GL_EXT_read_format_bgra: read RGBA, swap R/B on the CPU.

